From: Wisp buildtools
Subject: [PATCH] Backport interpreted Wasm proc macros to pinned Rust 1.83

Applies to oligamiq/rust cf327c2068549194a29160499c2ecafa9061e46e.
Adapted from the serialized-bridge approach in bjorn3/rust PR 157709,
head 2aa6abf53dc8c597d5f9c6e5f195c4080b5a61bf. This is a backport,
not a cherry-pick. The old typed Client and native ProcMacro ABI remain.

Use -Zwasm-proc-macros with macro modules compiled for
wasm32-unknown-unknown. Wasmi 0.40.0 runs inside rustc and forwards the
same-version proc_macro byte-buffer RPC. Macro declarations are queried
through scalar exports rather than cross-memory Rust layout assumptions.
Pointer-sized wire integers use checked u64 encoding.

Compiler, std/proc_macro, and proc-macro dependencies must be rebuilt
together. This patch is not compatible with the prebuilt bootstrap rustc.

